  "title": "Collocations",
  "emoji": "🤝",
  "parentNote": "Collocations are words that naturally go together — like \"make your bed\" (not \"do your bed\"). These are learned through reading and listening. Read stories together and point out common word pairs!",
  "learnBullets": [
    "What a **collocation** is — words that naturally go together",
    "Common collocations with **make**, **do**, **have**, **take**",
    "Word pairs that sound right together",
    "Choosing the right word partner"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**What is a Collocation?**\nA collocation is when certain words naturally go together. Native speakers just \"know\" these combinations.\n\n```\n✔️ make a mistake (correct)\n❌ do a mistake (wrong — sounds odd!)\n\n✔️ do homework (correct)\n❌ make homework (wrong)\n```\n\n**Common Collocations:**\n\n| With MAKE | With DO | With HAVE | With TAKE |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|-----------|\n| make the bed | do homework | have breakfast | take a bath |\n| make a cake | do the dishes | have fun | take a photo |\n| make friends | do your best | have a dream | take a rest |\n| make a wish | do exercise | have a cold | take a walk |\n| make noise | do a favour | have a party | take care |\n\n**Other Common Collocations:**\n\n| First Word | Goes With |\n|------------|-----------|\n| brush | teeth, hair |\n| catch | a ball, a cold, a bus |\n| tell | a story, a lie, the truth |\n| fast | food, asleep |\n| heavy | rain, traffic |\n| strong | wind, coffee |\n\n### 🧠 How to Choose the Right Collocation\n1. **Think:** Have I heard these words together before?\n2. **Say it:** Does it sound natural?\n3. **Remember:** Some combinations are fixed — learn them by heart!\n\n---",
